# Cursor-only execution depth

Parent MUST give every delegated task `DEPTH=VERIFY|PATCH|INVESTIGATE`. **Depth is not risk or model effort.** A money-sensitive but fully specified test is `VERIFY` with Grok 4.6 Medium, not a broad audit. Allowed model configurations remain in [Cursor cost policy](../../.agents/references/cursor-model-budget-policy.md).

- **VERIFY:** run the given command/procedure and record factual evidence. Read only the handoff, exact safety preconditions and necessary named runbook heading. Check git status; run the specified check once. No broad wiki/code discovery, speculative fixes, or unrelated tests. If blocked, make at most one error-directed diagnostic, record FAIL/NOT-RUN and stop. No silent promotion to PATCH.
- **PATCH:** implement an approved bounded change. Read the selected Change/route card, one relevant authority heading and 2–5 named source/test anchors. Then edit, run focused normal/negative proof, reconcile affected docs and required closure guards. Expand reading only for a concrete conflict, and say which uncertainty justified it.
- **INVESTIGATE:** only for an explicitly unresolved source/design question. Search narrowly, compare evidence and return the answer/owner or a proposed bounded Change. No unsolicited full-repo audit or speculative code edits.

**Stop searching** when owner, contract and negative case are known. Do not preload global skills, guard implementations or Markdown parsers. Run a guard first; inspect its implementation only if the error actually requires it. Prefer slices/symbols to large entire files. Do not spawn children to rediscover a parent's findings.

On a mismatch, report exact file/symbol, failed prerequisite and suggested narrow next action. Parent may issue a **new** scoped task; the child may not silently upgrade depth, model, speed or effort. Never High/Fast/Grok 4.7/Auto.

**Return:** DEPTH, command/edits, result/counts, actual checks, meaningful negative, blocker, source/commit and any justified extra reads. Unknown cost/tokens remain unknown.

**HK03 example:** 32-case Storyteller integration suite = `VERIFY`: check status and named disposable prerequisites, conditionally start the authorized local services, run the specified suite once, record pass/fail or NOT-RUN and commit the packet evidence. Don't start new engine/wiki research. Never reset protected DBs, delete volumes, run kind or call paid providers.
